From 3a18ee782abb5bc16fd6dfcefdbb9d05cc451734 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 359/488] soh: name the 20 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_ko.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 20 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Ko/z_en_ko.c; updating their references touches 3 files in total.

  * func_80A97BC0 -> EnKo_GetTrackYOffset
    deduced, confidence HIGH: returns the head-tracking yOffset for this
    Kokiri's type and forest quest state; Fado as adult is a fixed -20

  * func_80A97C7C -> EnKo_UsesGravity
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the caller runs Actor_UpdateBgCheckInfo and
    sets gravity -1 when this is true, gravity 0 when false

  * func_80A97D68 -> EnKo_UpdateLiftingRock
    deduced, confidence HIGH: loops gKokiriLiftingRockAnim while idle and
    switches to gKokiriWipingForeheadAnim to talk

  * func_80A97E18 -> EnKo_UpdateTrackNearbyPlayer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: fidgets, tracks head and torso within the talk
    angle, turns the whole body while talking, and stops tracking past
    lookDist

  * func_80A97EB0 -> EnKo_UpdateFidgetAndLook
    deduced, confidence HIGH: fidgets and tracks head and torso only while
    the player is within the talk angle, returning that test

  * func_80A97F20 -> EnKo_UpdateFacePlayer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: fidgets and turns the whole body toward the
    player unconditionally

  * func_80A97F70 -> EnKo_UpdateCuttingGrass
    deduced, confidence HIGH: loops gKokiriCuttingGrassAnim while idle and
    gKokiriBlockingAnim to talk

  * func_80A98034 -> EnKo_UpdatePunching
    deduced, confidence HIGH: loops gKokiriPunchingAnim while idle and
    gKokiriBlockingAnim to talk

  * func_80A98124 -> EnKo_UpdateFacePlayer2
    deduced, confidence HIGH: byte-identical duplicate of
    EnKo_UpdateFacePlayer, flagged as such by the comment above it, kept as
    its own symbol

  * func_80A98174 -> EnKo_UpdatePauseAnimToTalk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: freezes the current animation at frame 18
    while talking and resumes it at speed 1 afterwards

  * func_80A9877C -> EnKo_TrackPlayerAndTalk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: points the tracking at the player or the
    cutscene camera, runs Npc_UpdateTalking, and picks Fado's trade text in
    the Lost Woods

  * func_80A98CD8 -> EnKo_InitInteractInfo
    deduced, confidence HIGH: copies this type's sInteractInfo row into
    targetMode, lookDist and appearDist

  * func_80A98DB4 -> EnKo_UpdateModelAlpha
    deduced, confidence HIGH: fades the Kokiri out past appearDist in the
    forest scenes and drops targeting once nearly invisible

  * func_80A98ECC -> EnKo_UpdateByForestQuestState
    deduced, confidence HIGH: dispatches to the per-quest-state update,
    short-circuiting to EnKo_UpdateTrackNearbyPlayer for Fado in the Lost
    Woods

  * func_80A99048 -> EnKo_WaitForObjects
    deduced, confidence HIGH: holds until the animation and model objects
    load, then builds the skeleton and collider and installs the first real
    action

  * func_80A99384 -> EnKo_FadoWaitToTrade
    deduced, confidence HIGH: Fado's idle: starts the laugh on text 0x10B9
    and closes the textbox to hand over the saw on NPC_TALK_STATE_ACTION

  * func_80A99438 -> EnKo_FadoLaugh
    deduced, confidence HIGH: holds ENKO_ANIM_LAUGHING until the text
    changes or the trade begins

  * func_80A99504 -> EnKo_FadoGiveSaw
    deduced, confidence HIGH: offers GI_SAW until the player takes it

  * func_80A99560 -> EnKo_FadoFinishTrade
    deduced, confidence HIGH: continues into text 0x10B9, sets ITEMGETINF_31
    and returns to Fado's idle

  * func_80A995CC -> EnKo_OrbitHomeTowardPlayer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: parks the actor 80 units from its home
    position in the player's direction, facing the player, speeding the
    animation up with the angle swept

